.TH LOGIN-AUDIT 1 "2026-10-14" "SASD Freeware" "Unix Administration"
.SH NAME
login-audit \- read-only historical Linux login and failed-login overview
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B login-audit
[--kind success|failed|both] [--user NAME] [--limit 1..1000]
[--input-success FILE] [--input-failed FILE] [--null]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads util-linux last/lastb ISO-formatted text or, on Linux only, invokes
native last/lastb. Does not modify system login records. Source availability,
permissions, rotation and bounded 5000-entry samples limit completeness.
Zero reported rows do not prove that no login activity took place.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --kind success|failed|both
Select source, default both. Both is not globally time-sorted.
.TP
.B --user NAME
Exact case-sensitive account name filter.
.TP
.B --limit N
Output a maximum of N combined entries (default 100; maximum 1000).
.TP
.B --input-success FILE
Parse saved ISO-format last text from a regular non-symlink file.
.TP
.B --input-failed FILE
Parse saved ISO-format lastb text from a regular non-symlink file.
.TP
.B --null
Output six NUL-terminated fields: KIND USER TTY HOST LOGIN DETAILS.
.TP
.B --help, --version
Show metadata without accessing system history.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 sources processed; 1 malformed source rows (incomplete output);
2 invalid invocation; 3 source/backend unavailable or unsuccessful.
.SH SECURITY
Source records and reports can contain personal data. No root privileges
are requested or granted by this tool. Native macOS/BSD history is unsupported.
.SH SEE ALSO
last(1), lastb(1), wtmp(5), btmp(5)
.SH AUTHOR
SASD Freeware contributors.
